WEBVTT

NOTE The Gold Rush (1925) - Riah TV captions

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:08.490
During the Great Gold Rush of
Alaska, men in thousands came
from all parts of the world.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:16.490
Many were ignorant of the
hardships before them, the
intense cold, the lack of food —

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:24.500
and a journey through regions of
ice and snow was a problem that
awaited them.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.700
[music]

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:46.750
The Chilkoot Pass. A test of
man's endurance. At this point
many turned back discouraged,
whilst others went bravely on.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:00.750
The Top of the Pass.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.500
Three days from anywhere.
A Lone Prospector.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.750
Another lone prospector.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:25.500
Big Jim's Lucky Strike.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:42.250
"I've found it! I've found
it! A Mountain of Gold."

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.250
Then came a storm.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.750
A Lone Cabin.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.000
And a lone man.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.000
"Get out of here!"

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:31.000
"Get out, the pair of you."

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:47.500
"There's another bullet
left, so beat it!"

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.250
"I'll stay right here!"

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:13.500
The storm raged for days.

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:19.750
The three men were hungry.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.750
"I must have food!"

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:23.750
"What are you eating?"

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:27.000
"We must get food. One of
us must brave that storm."

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:34.250
"We'll cut the cards,
and the low man goes."

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:28.500
The Hand of the Law.

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:37.750
Indifferent to his comrade's
plight, Black Larsen stumbles on
the claim of Big Jim McKay.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:54.500
Waiting for relief.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:38.000
"I thought you was a chicken."

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:00.250
"I'm sorry, I must be crazy."

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:39.500
Chicken or no chicken, his
friend looks appetizing.

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:41.000
Then came the parting of the
ways. One to his secret mine.
The other to his fate.

00:25:09.750 --> 00:25:14.500
Direct to the mountain of gold.

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:10.000
The North. A law unto itself.

00:26:53.500 --> 00:27:03.250
One of the many cities in the
Far North, built overnight
during the great gold rush.

00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:19.250
Jack, the ladies' man.

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:06.750
A disappointed prospector.

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:25.000
The only gold he made
with pick and shovel.

00:28:33.500 --> 00:28:41.500
A night in the Monte
Carlo dance hall.

00:31:59.750 --> 00:32:03.500
"What's wrong with
you tonight, dear?"

00:32:06.500 --> 00:32:08.750
"I guess I'm bored."

00:32:10.750 --> 00:32:17.750
"If I could only meet someone
worth while — I'm so tired of
this place."

00:33:35.250 --> 00:33:38.250
"How's the little spitfire?"

00:33:49.750 --> 00:33:53.250
"Oh quit that stuff
and have a drink."

00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:13.250
"You're pretty fresh, ain't ya?"

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:29.250
"Come on now, me and
you are going to dance."

00:34:35.000 --> 00:34:37.250
"Hey you! Come here!"

00:34:53.500 --> 00:34:56.500
"Do you mind dancing with me?"

00:34:58.750 --> 00:35:03.500
"You see, I'm very
particular who I dance with."

00:39:45.000 --> 00:39:51.000
The following morning.

00:39:56.500 --> 00:40:02.000
Hank Curtis' cabin. Within a
stone's throw of the dance hall.

00:40:25.250 --> 00:40:28.000
One way of getting breakfast.

00:42:17.000 --> 00:42:27.250
Big Jim McKay, owing to the blow
he had received, lost his memory
and wandered aimlessly on.

00:42:43.500 --> 00:42:50.000
Hank Curtis and his partner
prepare for a trip to their
mine.

00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:04.000
"Who is the little fellow?"

00:43:05.500 --> 00:43:10.500
"Just someone to take care
of the cabin while I'm away."

00:43:20.500 --> 00:43:23.500
"Don't forget to feed the mule."

00:43:50.000 --> 00:43:54.000
Away from the dance hall.

00:45:19.000 --> 00:45:23.000
"I haven't seen you since
we danced together."

00:47:48.000 --> 00:47:50.750
"I guess you're lonesome here."

00:47:56.500 --> 00:48:01.000
"Why don't you invite
us to dinner sometime?"

00:48:55.250 --> 00:48:59.000
"Will you really
come to dinner?"

00:49:01.500 --> 00:49:06.500
"Oh yes! Let's make it
New Year's Eve, girls."

00:49:08.000 --> 00:49:11.250
"Very well, eight
o'clock New Year's Eve."

00:50:21.500 --> 00:50:23.500
"I left my gloves."

00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:44.250
To make possible the New Year's
dinner, he begged, borrowed and
shovelled.

00:52:29.750 --> 00:52:34.750
New Year's Eve.

00:52:44.000 --> 00:52:46.750
Five minutes to eight.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:33.750
"I'm so h-h-happy
— Oh, I can't —"

00:58:08.000 --> 00:58:12.500
"Our old friend Scotty
will sing Auld Lang Syne."

01:00:18.750 --> 01:00:22.750
"That reminds me, our
little friend the tramp."

01:00:24.250 --> 01:00:28.000
"Let's go up and have
some fun with him."

01:00:46.000 --> 01:00:47.750
"Do you love me?"

01:01:25.750 --> 01:01:29.250
"You go first. We'll scare
the wits out of him."

01:02:15.000 --> 01:02:19.000
"Well it doesn't
matter. Kiss me."

01:02:32.750 --> 01:02:37.000
"The joke has gone
too far, let's go!"

01:02:45.250 --> 01:02:47.000
"Why don't you kiss me?"

01:03:11.000 --> 01:03:17.250
The recorder's office the next
day. Big Jim McKay wanders into
town.

01:03:46.500 --> 01:03:50.000
"I have a mountain of gold."

01:03:52.500 --> 01:03:55.000
"Where is this place?"

01:04:04.500 --> 01:04:06.750
"I can't remember."

01:04:13.000 --> 01:04:21.500
"The Cabin! That's it! If I only
knew the way to the Cabin, I
could find the mine."

01:04:28.750 --> 01:04:32.250
"I'm sorry Jim, but
we're very busy."

01:04:52.750 --> 01:04:59.750
In the dance hall that night.

01:06:52.750 --> 01:06:57.500
"Give that bum this note, and
don't tell him I sent it."

01:07:26.500 --> 01:07:27.750
"Have you seen Georgia?"

01:07:43.000 --> 01:07:44.250
THE CABIN!

01:08:05.500 --> 01:08:09.250
"The Cabin! The Cabin!
Take me to the Cabin."

01:08:10.250 --> 01:08:15.250
"Take me to the Cabin and I'll
make you a millionaire in less
than a month."

01:08:30.750 --> 01:08:33.750
"Georgia, I got your note —"

01:08:38.250 --> 01:08:40.500
"— and now I'm going
to make good —"

01:09:09.750 --> 01:09:16.000
After a long and
tedious journey.

01:09:25.750 --> 01:09:27.250
"The Cabin at last!"

01:09:48.500 --> 01:09:53.000
"Bring in the eats, and in the
morning we'll start for the
mine."

01:11:25.000 --> 01:11:29.500
Man proposes, but
a storm disposes.

01:12:07.000 --> 01:12:17.500
And as our slumbering heroes
slept throughout the storm —
fate guided them to a spot where
all was calm.

01:12:58.000 --> 01:13:01.000
Preparing for breakfast.

01:15:33.000 --> 01:15:35.750
"I'll see what's outside."

01:16:46.000 --> 01:16:49.000
"Don't move! Don't breathe!"

01:18:35.000 --> 01:18:38.750
"My Claim! My Claim! At
last I've found my claim."

01:19:22.250 --> 01:19:25.500
"Look! We're rich!
We're millionaires."

01:19:35.000 --> 01:19:44.000
Good-bye Alaska. Homeward
bound on the good ship Success.

01:19:47.750 --> 01:19:50.750
"Make way for the
Multi-millionaires."

01:21:04.750 --> 01:21:10.500
"The press is publishing a story
of your career. Would you kindly
pose for us in your mining
clothes?"

01:21:28.750 --> 01:21:31.500
"No no, not the
nails — the corns."

01:21:55.750 --> 01:21:59.000
Everything but Georgia.

01:22:10.250 --> 01:22:13.250
Searching for a stowaway.

01:22:19.500 --> 01:22:25.000
"He's in the steerage here
somewhere. If I find him I'll
put him in irons."

01:24:18.500 --> 01:24:22.000
"So you're the stowaway —
I've been looking for you."

01:24:23.750 --> 01:24:27.250
"Please, please, don't put him
in irons. I'll pay his fare."

01:24:43.250 --> 01:24:47.500
"A stowaway, heck! That's Big
Jim's partner, the
Multi-millionaire."

01:25:00.250 --> 01:25:03.250
"James. Make arrangements
for another guest."

01:25:14.500 --> 01:25:17.500
"Excuse me, Sir —
Who is the Lady?"

01:25:57.750 --> 01:26:01.000
"Gee! This will make
a wonderful story."

01:26:15.750 --> 01:26:18.000
"Oh! You've spoilt the picture."
